DRILL CONFIG — FULL SOURCE, so qa-a8573597 can recreate and re-run the mutants without my temp file (msg-29ed2912 says they will run them). ZERO ON-DISK MUTATION: in-memory Vite `transform`, `enforce: "pre"`. Written to `%TEMP%/moe-drill-c055f6af-worker-a1cf5270.mjs` — out of tree, so no backup and no SHA256 restore proof is owed. Run from `apps/daemon` as `MOE_DRILL_MUTANT=<name> npx vitest run --root . --config <path> src/planning/approval-activation-graph-absence.test.ts`. Clean control is the SAME command with `--config package.json` and no env var.

```js
const SEP = String.fromCharCode(92);
const MUTANT = process.env.MOE_DRILL_MUTANT;

const JOURNEY = "apps/daemon/src/gates-journey-fixtures.ts";
const PROJECTION = "apps/daemon/src/planning/active-graph-projection.ts";

const ANCHOR = "  approvePlan(store, sealed.runId);";
const IMPORT = "import { seedActivationGraph as drillSeed } from \"./activation/activation-world-fixtures.js\";\n";
const ABSENT = "return refuse(\"ACTIVE_GRAPH_ABSENT\");";
const SPLIT = "return refuse(\"ACTIVE_GRAPH_SPLIT_BRAIN\");";
const LAYER = "    layer: ACTIVE_GRAPH_PROJECTION_LAYER,";
const WRONG = "    layer: \"CORE_GRAPH_REVISION_REPLAY\",";

const KNOWN = ["afterapproval", "wrongcode", "wronglayer"];
if (!KNOWN.includes(String(MUTANT))) {
  throw new Error("DRILL_UNKNOWN_MUTANT_" + String(MUTANT));
}

export default {
  plugins: [{
    enforce: "pre",
    name: "moe-drill-c055f6af",
    transform(code, id) {
      const path = id.split(SEP).join("/");
      if (MUTANT === "afterapproval" && path.endsWith(JOURNEY)) {
        if (!code.includes(ANCHOR)) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING_approvePlan");
        return { code: IMPORT + code.replace(ANCHOR, ANCHOR + "\n  drillSeed(store);"), map: null };
      }
      if (MUTANT === "wrongcode" && path.endsWith(PROJECTION)) {
        if (!code.includes(ABSENT)) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING_absentRefusal");
        return { code: code.split(ABSENT).join(SPLIT), map: null };
      }
      if (MUTANT === "wronglayer" && path.endsWith(PROJECTION)) {
        if (!code.includes(LAYER)) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING_layerField");
        return { code: code.split(LAYER).join(WRONG), map: null };
      }
      return null;
    },
  }],
  test: { include: ["src/**/*.test.ts"] },
};
```

NOTES ON THE SHAPE, all learned the hard way and encoded above: no `import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config"` — it does not resolve from %TEMP%; a plain object default export works. No backslash literal anywhere — `String.fromCharCode(92)` instead, because the heredoc eats it. Every mutant anchors on an EXACT literal and THROWS when the anchor is missing, so a drifted anchor cannot transform nothing and be misread as "the arm did not red". An unrecognised `MOE_DRILL_MUTANT` throws at config load rather than silently running the unmutated tree.

RESTORE PROOF (nothing to restore, proven rather than asserted):
`git hash-object <path>` == `git rev-parse HEAD:<path>` for both drilled files at the end of the drill —
  apps/daemon/src/gates-journey-fixtures.ts        0a34decfd3ed8b8669e0e8dfa7f491ab60191529 (both)
  apps/daemon/src/planning/active-graph-projection.ts  764ad0ab6f6ed78780a5f4756f2e4a18bab88878 (both)
`git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- apps/daemon/src` before, during and after listed only this row's three paths.
